        "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $K:X\\to Y$ be a compact operator of infinite rank between real or complex Hilbert spaces over one scalar field. Let $(s_j,v_j,u_j)_{j\\ge1}$ be a positive singular system with $s_j>0$, $s_j\\to0$, $\\|v_j\\|_X=\\|u_j\\|_Y=1$, and $Kv_j=s_ju_j$. For $\\rho>0$ let $M_\\rho=X_{1,\\rho}(K)=\\{|K|w:w\\in X,\\ \\|w\\|_X\\le\\rho\\}$ and define $\\varepsilon_K(M_\\rho,\\delta)=\\sup\\{\\|x\\|_X:x\\in M_\\rho,\\ \\|Kx\\|_Y\\le\\delta\\}$. Then $\\varepsilon_K(M_\\rho,\\delta)\\le\\sqrt{\\rho\\delta}$ for every $\\delta\\ge0$, with equality at $\\delta_j=\\rho s_j^2$ for each $j$, witnessed by $x_j=\\rho s_jv_j$. Although $K^\\dagger$ is discontinuous on its full domain, this modulus tends to zero on the restricted source class $M_\\rho$; this conditional stability makes no claim of universal noise-level-free convergence.",
